Members of the IACG are involved in standards development and research with the goal toward informing IACG members of activity that affects and is affected by the practice of information architecture.

The following working groups discuss and are informed by IA work:

## Internet Safety Labs
https://www.internetsafetylabs.org
Developing specifications for safe software, including a taxonomy of harmful product behavior and a digital harms dictionary. Information architecture principles inform this work.

## Kantara Intiative
https://www.kantarainitiative.org
Participating in work groups as an advocate for technology users, developing use cases and mental models. 

## User Experience Professionals Association
https://www.uxpa.org
Providing comment for ISO drafts. 

## Open Voice Network
https://www.openvoicenetwork.org
Providing guidance on interaction and mental models of interoperable voice systems.
